History: "invalid initializer '__pair1_'" in __tree; bodyless-member
family (__emplace_unique_key_args dropped); three cvise degeneracy
classes (parked).  Round-25 root pair (2026-08-08): (a) fifth
TT-instance consumer -- disambiguate_template_classes' instance
fallback could not find a NAMESPACE-scope template (root-scope
RECURSIVE lookup does not descend into namespaces; fixed by looking
up in the instance scope's grandparent per [namespace.qual]);
(b) member-alias own-parameter capture ([temp.local]/1) extended to
references nested in pointer declarators and template-id arguments
(pointer_traits<_Tp*>'s `rebind = _Up*`,
allocator_traits' `rebind_alloc =
__allocator_traits_rebind_t<allocator_type, _Other>`) -- previously
only top-level bare references were protected, so `_Up`/`_Other`
captured unrelated enclosing bindings (int), unique_ptr's deleter
became __tree_node_destructor<allocator<int>>, get() returned int*,
and __emplace_unique_key_args' conversion threw (swallowed by the
system-header SFINAE guard), dropping insert semantics entirely.
Needs --object-bits 12 past "too many addressed objects".
